{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N44rsoN5JuJyU9gjYhXUDC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd042-whoami\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/whoami: Print Effective User Name\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Scripts and interactive sessions use whoami as a quick check for the effective user identity,\n6\t  particularly when verifying privilege escalation or drop. The utility is deliberately minimal:\n7\t  it prints one name and exits. The macOS BSD whoami and GNU whoami behave identically for the\n8\t  core case, but differ in --help and --version handling. The Go implementation must match the\n9\t  Homebrew GNU reference binary (gwhoami, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by\n10\t  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n11\t\n12\tgoals:\n13\t  - G1: Print the effective username of the current process followed by a newline.\n14\t  - G2: Reject any extra operands with an error message and nonzero exit.\n15\t\n16\trequirements:\n17\t  R1:\n18\t    title: Default behavior\n19\t    items:\n20\t      - R1.1:\n21\t          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print the effective username (equivalent to id -un) followed by a newline and exit 0.\n22\t      - R1.2:\n23\t          text: The username must reflect the effective UID, not the real UID, matching the behavior of gwhoami after su or sudo.\n24\t\n25\t  R2:\n26\t    title: Error handling\n27\t    items:\n28\t      - R2.1:\n29\t          text: If any extra operand is provided (beyond --help and --version), must print an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n30\t      - R2.2:\n31\t          text: Must not accept any flags other than --help and --version. Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n32\t\n33\t  R3:\n34\t    title: Differential testing\n35\t    items:\n36\t      - R3.1:\n37\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (gwhoami) via pkg/testutils.\n38\t      - R3.2:\n39\t          text: \"Tests must cover: normal invocation (no arguments), extra operand error, and unknown flag error.\"\n40\t      - R3.3:\n41\t          text: Tests must verify that the output matches the effective username returned by the system.\n42\t\n43\tnon_goals:\n44\t  - cmd/whoami does not accept a USER argument; it always reports the current process identity.\n45\t  - cmd/whoami does not print the UID, GID, or group memberships; use cmd/id for that.\n46\t  - cmd/whoami does not support -u or any other selection flags.\n47\t\n48\tacceptance_criteria:\n49\t  - id: AC1\n50\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/whoami prints the current effective username, matching gwhoami.\"\n51\t    traces:\n52\t      - R1.1\n53\t      - R1.2\n54\t  - id: AC2\n55\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/whoami extraarg exits 1 with an error message to stderr, matching gwhoami.\"\n56\t    traces:\n57\t      - R1.1\n58\t      - R2.1\n59\t      - R2.2\n60\t      - R3.1\n61\t      - R3.2\n62\t  - id: AC3\n63\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gwhoami passes for normal invocation and error cases.\"\n64\t    traces:\n65\t      - R2.1\n66\t      - R2.2\n67\t      - R3.1\n68\t      - R3.2\n69\t  - id: AC4\n70\t    criterion: \"cmd/whoami compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n71\t    traces:\n72\t      - R1.1\n73\t      - R1.2\n74\t      - R2.1\n75\t      - R2.2\n76\t      - R3.1\n77\t      - R3.2\n78\t      - R3.3\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6410be5e-ecf6-4c86-a8a2-afd4192393ff","uuid":"1d02b589-8dba-4437-85a2-825e322f8c25","timestamp":"2026-05-20T13:37:27.311Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5355/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd042-whoami.yaml","content":"id: srd042-whoami\ntitle: \"cmd/whoami: Print Effective User Name\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Scripts and interactive sessions use whoami as a quick check for the effective user identity,\n  particularly when verifying privilege escalation or drop. The utility is deliberately minimal:\n  it prints one name and exits. The macOS BSD whoami and GNU whoami behave identically for the\n  core case, but differ in --help and --version handling. The Go implementation must match the\n  Homebrew GNU reference binary (gwhoami, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by\n  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Print the effective username of the current process followed by a newline.\n  - G2: Reject any extra operands with an error message and nonzero exit.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print the effective username (equivalent to id -un) followed by a newline and exit 0.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: The username must reflect the effective UID, not the real UID, matching the behavior of gwhoami after su or sudo.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Error handling\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: If any extra operand is provided (beyond --help and --version), must print an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must not accept any flags other than --help and --version. Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (gwhoami) via pkg/testutils.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: normal invocation (no arguments), extra operand error, and unknown flag error.\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Tests must verify that the output matches the effective username returned by the system.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/whoami does not accept a USER argument; it always reports the current process identity.\n  - cmd/whoami does not print the UID, GID, or group memberships; use cmd/id for that.\n  - cmd/whoami does not support -u or any other selection flags.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/whoami prints the current effective username, matching gwhoami.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/whoami extraarg exits 1 with an error message to stderr, matching gwhoami.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gwhoami passes for normal invocation and error cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/whoami compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n","numLines":79,"startLine":1,"totalLines":79}}}
