{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler stitch task (#5355) to implement `cmd/whoami/main.go` for the go-unix-utils project. The task is titled \"[stitch] srd042-whoami R1.1, R1.2, R2.1, R2.2 (implementation)\". The utility must print the effective username to stdout followed by a newline, support --help and --version flags, reject extra operands and unknown flags with errors to stderr, and install a SIGPIPE handler. The implementation must match GNU `gwhoami` behavior and follow strict coding standards defined in the execution constitution and go style constitution.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU `whoami` utility\n   - Differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binary (`gwhoami`)\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Effective UID lookup (not real UID) via Go's `os/user` package\n   - Strict coding standards: 40-line function limit, SPDX copyright header, no magic strings\n   - Git managed externally — no git commands allowed\n   - Must write all files before building/testing\n   - `go build -o bin/whoami ./cmd/whoami/` for compilation\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd042-whoami.yaml` (READ)\n     - Source of truth for whoami requirements\n     - R1.1: Print effective username + newline, exit 0\n     - R1.2: Reflect effective UID (matches behavior after su/sudo)\n     - R2.1: Extra operands → error to stderr, exit 1\n     - R2.2: Only --help and --version accepted; unknown flags → error to stderr, exit 1\n     - Non-goals: no USER argument, no UID/GID output, no -u flag\n   \n   - `cmd/whoami/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - The main deliverable — whoami utility implementation\n     - Must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` first in main()\n     - Must use `os/user.Current()` for effective username\n     - Must handle --help, --version, reject extra operands and unknown flags\n\n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (PROVIDED IN CONTEXT)\n     - Contains `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` — installs SIGPIPE handler that exits 0\n     - Import path: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n\n   - Existing cmd/ patterns (from context):\n     - All cmd/ utilities call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n     - Copyright header: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n     - Outputs to os.Stdout, errors to os.Stderr\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — implementation has not started.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand the full specification before implementing\n   - The whoami utility is straightforward: get effective username via `os/user.Current()`, print it, handle flags and errors\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The first (and only substantive) user message is the massive task prompt containing: role definition, repository file list, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source code), requirement states, task definition, execution constitution, go style constitution, constraints, description with requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, shared protocols, and package contracts.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/whoami/main.go` with the whoami implementation\n   - Verify compilation with `go build -o bin/whoami ./cmd/whoami/`\n   - Verify with `go vet ./cmd/whoami/...`\n   - Verify the binary works (prints username, handles --help, --version, extra args)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd042-whoami.yaml` and was about to implement `cmd/whoami/main.go`. The SRD confirmed:\n   - R1.1: Print effective username + newline, exit 0\n   - R1.2: Must use effective UID\n   - R2.1: Extra operands → error + exit 1\n   - R2.2: Only --help/--version; unknown flags → error + exit 1\n   \n   The task requires creating a single file `cmd/whoami/main.go` that:\n   - Starts with SPDX copyright header\n   - Calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` \n   - Parses only --help and --version flags\n   - Rejects extra operands and unknown flags\n   - Uses `os/user.Current()` to get effective username\n   - Prints username to stdout with newline, exits 0\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Create `cmd/whoami/main.go` using the Write tool. The implementation should:\n   - Follow the task description: \"files: path: cmd/whoami/main.go, action: create\"\n   - Implement all 4 requirements (R1-R4 mapping to srd042 R1.1, R1.2, R2.1, R2.2)\n   - Follow design decisions D1 (SIGPIPE handler) and D2 (stdout/stderr)\n   - Then verify with `go build -o bin/whoami ./cmd/whoami/` and `go vet ./cmd/whoami/...` per acceptance criteria AC1 and AC5\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5355/6410be5e-ecf6-4c86-a8a2-afd4192393ff.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6410be5e-ecf6-4c86-a8a2-afd4192393ff","uuid":"573d4379-9e47-4fdc-bf7a-dbb4297f4492","timestamp":"2026-05-20T13:38:02.655Z","isSynthetic":true}
